Two corrections to the plan's own record, both because the code moved past it.

P2.T1 was recorded as "blocked on that decision" — a fork between registering the field
as a String and building Map values in codegen. That fork was false: codegen has no Map
value at all and the layout's "Map" tag had no consumer, so serializing was the only
option that did not mean inventing Map values and readers under a scraper task. The
blocker note is superseded with the measurements that replaced it, the two defects the
proof caught (a probe whose JSON-LD braces became string interpolation, and a first
commit that swept 184 lines of rustfmt churn around a four-site edit), and its evidence.

P2.T3 said "exercise both natives". Only one is bound — P2.T2 was re-scoped out — so the
acceptance is now stated for StructuredData.extract alone, with the three graded
assertions copied from the harness that established them for this class, and open_graph
excluded by name because the interpreter and the compiled path hold different
representations of it.

P2.T4's refusal arms were listed as blank seed URL and malformed HTML; those belong to
the crawler/sitemap natives, not this one. Corrected to the arm this native has.
